{
	"_comment": "The Exchange: townsfolk post work in the paper. A request's 'value' is what one item (or creature) is worth in emeralds, and its count range is sized as a week's work; the job's worth is count x value. The reward is worth that times 'premium' (drawn between the two), so the pay is generous: emeralds, or one of the character's 'prizes' or the 'commonPrizes' that comes out near that value, in master-trade goods - enchanted books, diamonds, diamond gear, golden apples. 'tier' is how far along a player must be: 0 starting out, 1 has found iron, 2 has been to the Nether, 3 has been to the End. A prize's 'max' is how many may be given at once; 'enchant' and 'level' make an enchanted book or enchant the item. Names and towns come from names.json; 'id' picks the profession's name list. Each reader gets 'deliveries' notices from different trades and 'slayings' jobs for the Watch.",
